10 REM ** DRUNKARD'S WALK **
20 REM ** A ONE-DIMENSIONAL RANDOM WALK, IN THE MANNER OF THE **
30 REM ** LISTINGS IN D. AHL (ED.), 101 BASIC COMPUTER GAMES, **
40 REM ** DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORP., MAYNARD MASS., 1973 **
50 REM
60 REM ** THE STREET RUNS FROM THE CANAL (0) TO HIS HOUSE (40). **
70 REM ** THE TAVERN STANDS AT 20.  AT EACH STROKE OF THE CLOCK **
80 REM ** HE STAGGERS ONE LAMP-POST LEFT OR RIGHT.  THE THEOREM **
90 REM ** SAYS HE ARRIVES SOMEWHERE WITH PROBABILITY ONE. **
100 REM ** THE THEOREM DOES NOT SAY WHERE. **
110 REM
120 RANDOMIZE TIMER
130 PRINT "CLOSING TIME."
140 PRINT "THE DRUNKARD LEAVES THE TAVERN AT LAMP-POST 20."
150 PRINT "HIS HOUSE IS AT 40.  THE CANAL IS AT 0."
160 PRINT
170 LET P = 20
180 LET T = 0
190 REM ** THE NIGHT WEARS ON **
200 LET T = T + 1
210 IF RND < .5 THEN 240
220 LET P = P + 1
230 GOTO 250
240 LET P = P - 1
250 PRINT TAB(P + 1);"*"
260 IF P = 0 THEN 320
270 IF P = 40 THEN 360
280 IF T = 500 THEN 400
290 GOTO 200
300 REM
310 REM ** ENDINGS, OF WHICH NO KIND IS GOOD **
320 PRINT
330 PRINT "AFTER "; T; " STEPS, THE CANAL."
340 PRINT "THE WATER IS PATIENT.  IT HAS WAITED ALL EVENING."
350 GOTO 430
360 PRINT
370 PRINT "AFTER "; T; " STEPS HE FINDS HIS OWN FRONT DOOR."
380 PRINT "BY MORNING HE REMEMBERS NOTHING, AND SETS OUT AGAIN."
390 GOTO 430
400 PRINT
410 PRINT "AFTER 500 STEPS THE CLOCK GIVES UP THE COUNT."
420 PRINT "HE LIES DOWN BENEATH LAMP-POST "; P; " TO SLEEP IN THE SNOW."
430 END
